From: Hoki local maintainers <code@lukasrieger.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: bgcom: recover from resume timeout without BUG

A Blackghost subsystem restart can enter runtime resume while the peripheral
is unavailable. After 100 failed polls bgcom_resume_l() calls BUG(), killing
the application processor before its existing soft-reset/error path runs.

Keep the bounded timeout, diagnostic GPIO reads, soft reset and -ETIMEDOUT
return. Remove the unconditional fatal assertion: a peripheral failing to
wake is not an unrecoverable kernel invariant violation.

Observed on Hoki kernel 4.14.206 after restarting the Sidekick HAL: the
failure diagnostics are immediately followed by an undefined-instruction
Oops in bgcom_resume_l on ssr_wq. This fixes that explicit panic path; it does
not establish why the peripheral originally stopped responding.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/bgcom_spi.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/bgcom_spi.c
@@ -573,7 +573,7 @@
 				__func__, gpio_get_value(95));
 		pr_err("%s: gpio#97 value is: %d\n",
 				__func__, gpio_get_value(97));
-		BUG();
+		/* A peripheral timeout must not crash the application processor. */
 		bg_soft_reset();
 		return -ETIMEDOUT;
 	}
